    <string name="about_mode_running_title">Running — Force Stop</string>
    <string name="about_mode_running">Shows apps running in the foreground or recently used. Tap an app to force-stop it: it is immediately terminated and removed from recents. With the system-apps toggle you see everything, including core services — handle with care.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_restricted_title">Restricted — Protected list</string>
    <string name="about_mode_restricted">Apps on this list are never stopped by the magic button or batch actions. Use it to protect your launcher, keyboard, wallet, and essential services. Defaults are detected automatically from your device.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_blocked_title">Blocked — Persistent block</string>
    <string name="about_mode_blocked">Blocked apps are suspended, have their background permissions cut, and are placed in the restricted standby bucket. The watcher service keeps reapplying the block every minute so they cannot come back on their own — even Play Services.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_frozen_title">Frozen — Full disable</string>
    <string name="about_mode_frozen">Freezing fully disables the app (pm disable-user). It disappears from the drawer, cannot start at all, and uses no memory. The strongest option. Requires Shizuku. Unfreeze at any time to restore it.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_schedule_title">Schedule — Automatic cleanups</string>
    <string name="about_mode_schedule">Create groups with a name, a set of apps, and a time. Choose the mode: force-stop, block, restrict, or freeze. Runs once or on repeat by weekday or interval. The alarm fires even with the screen off.</string>
    <string name="about_mode_bubble_title">Magic Bubble</string>
    <string name="about_mode_bubble">A floating button that stays on top of every app. Tap it once to stop all non-protected apps. Hold it for 2 seconds to jump straight to bubble settings. Drag to position it anywhere on screen — position is remembered.</string>
